{"title":"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jesse cuts a circular paper disk of radius 12 along two radii to form two sectors, the smaller having a central angle of 120 degrees. He makes two circular cones, using each sector to form the lateral surface of a cone. What is the ratio of the volume of the smaller cone to that of the larger?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/f/59fe4cad279f9ab6ceb23db4c54e2a56c912de9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A)} \\frac{1}{8} \\qquad \\text{(B)} \\frac{1}{4} \\qquad \\text{(C)} \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10} \\qquad \\text{(D)} \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{6} \\qquad \\text{(E)} \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"376\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's find the volume of the smaller cone first. We know that the circumference of the paper disk is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/7/ca72da509d0e888f69331dc91184a176fef7dae5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, so the circumference of the smaller cone would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/7/717f10c8be94d37b48a1b9e38677ad02957ba90d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{120}{360} \\times 24\\pi = 8\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"126\" height=\"37\" />. This means that the radius of the smaller cone is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since the radius of the paper disk is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the slant height of the smaller cone would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. By the Pythagorean Theorem, the height of the cone is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/2/df2ac941e02de0cafe92b319f1046348c1e57d0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{12^2-4^2}=8\\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"139\" height=\"21\" />. Thus, the volume of the smaller cone is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/5/415c06e5bd4e3a5c92107f84d8c4252cfd0ab65d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{3} \\times 4^2\\pi \\times 8\\sqrt{2}=\\dfrac{128\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"208\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we need to find the volume of the larger cone. Using the same reason as above, we get that the radius is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the slant height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. By the Pythagorean Theorem again, the height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/7/d1768a4753badeaf5cea89030367958ead46a571.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{12^2-8^2}=4\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"137\" height=\"19\" />. Thus, the volume of the larger cone is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/9/9b96b7fa346d44a96fecfa3387dafc7e665cf109.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{3} \\times 8^2\\pi \\times 4\\sqrt{5} = \\dfrac{256\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"208\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>The question asked for the ratio of the volume of the smaller cone to the larger cone. We need to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/8/bd8290fead31e944490375ca3ec4db527cf84877.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{\\dfrac{128\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\pi}{\\dfrac{256\\sqrt{5}}{3}\\pi}=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -39px\" width=\"130\" height=\"87\" /> after simplifying, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/c/1acc2d8106aba563c4db2d35b9127e61ecde0238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(C)  \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"77\" height=\"53\" /> .\n</p>\n<ul><li>A side note</li></ul>\n<p>We can first simplify the volume ratio: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/4/154f95f2c3f713e901cab92c31512b4ecb74b0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{V_1}{V_2} = \\frac{(r_1)^2 \\cdot h_1}{(r_2)^2 \\cdot h_2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"122\" height=\"43\" /> Now we can find the GENERAL formulas for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> based on the original circle radius and angle to cut out, then we can substitute the appropriate numbers, which gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/2/792daa030c96693198f143f9176bf888b7ca25cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C.$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B\">2012 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2012 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017014843\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.032 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.050 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 186/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 363